{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1011468-naughty-pc-s-and-the-guardians-when-do-the-gotv-step-in-and-what-do-they-do","id":1011468,"title":"Naughty PC's and the Guardians: When do the GOTV step in, and what do they do?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-03T06:10:36-08:00","id":1011468,"title":"Naughty PC's and the Guardians: When do the GOTV step in, and what do they do?","content":"Of all the Orders, how the Guardians of the Veil operate is one of the fuzzier concepts I have, and were I to ST, I would like to know how the operate especially as it pertains to the PC's.<br /> <br /> First of all, what kinds of activities bring the attention of the Guardians?<br /> Paradox? Does it matter whether the paradox is contained released?<br /> How often would someone have to tempt paradox before the Guardians took interest? <br /> What about the Lex Magica? The Guardians seem to be more concerned about Wisdom than the Lex, but it seems like any action they might take would preferably be within the Lex... It's kind of hard to justify taking action against a mage, if by the Lex they've done no wrong.<br /> <br /> Then, how do the Guardians find out? Obviously they aren't omniscient, so it's not as though they are going to swoop down like Batman out of nowhere the moment the PC's get out of line. But at the same time, they ARE mages, and MIGHT be scrying on the PC's, or they might not. How do you determine whether the PC's are being watched by the Guardians?<br /> <br /> What if one of the PC's is a Guardian, but is lying down on the job?<br /> <br /> And when the Guardians do come down on the PC's, how will they do it? Will they kindly ask them to stop? Bring the Lex down on them? Try to teach the PC a lesson? Take the PC on a long walk down a short pier in concrete shoes?<br /> <br /> And as a Storyteller, how do you balance the conflicting philosophies of: &quot;The players' actions should have consequences&quot; versus &quot;Don't try to punish your players&quot; while still being true to the setting and the presence of the Guardians of the Veil?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1078-froggy711","name":"Froggy711","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1078_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T08:06:14-08:00","id":1011501,"title":"","content":"The Guardians of the Veil are the secret police of Atlantis, so the legend goes, and that's about the role they <i>try</i> and fulfill. In their ideal world, the Guardians are omniscient; watching their fellow Awakened (including each other) for signs of moral failure and correcting it, with Wise advice if possible and long knives if not. Their fellow Awakened hate them out of ritual necessity, for none can be allowed to love their duty, but accept them and thank them for their grim service.<br /> <br /> In practice, pretty much none of these things are true.<br /> <br /> The expectation a neophyte might have of the Guardians is that they're sitting in their hideouts all day, scrying other Awakened, tracking them, building webs of information. The solution to a nail in the mind of all unexperienced Awakened is the magical hammer. In practice, though, this is a <i>terrible</i> way to collect information on fellow Awakened because they can all sense when magic is being cast upon them. Not to mention that you need sympathetic connection to them which is harder than it sounds to get. And on top of that, odds are good that your scrying window <i>isn't</i> going to catch anything heinous because you can't really maintain it 24/7; you've got your own shit to do if nothing else.<br /> <br /> Instead, Guardians have to rely on tools other than their magic (at least in a direct manner) to get information on their fellow Awakened. This means relying on contacts and omens as signs of danger.<br /> <br /> Your average Guardian has a roster of Awakened to spy on provided by their Caucus, on whom they maintain dossiers (usually mentally; writing things down is a dangerous risk). To build those dossiers, they need to rely on the aforementioned sources.<br /> <br /> Contacts are people - Awakened or not; sometimes even stretching the definition of &quot;person&quot; - whom the Guardian can rely on for information on the target for one reason or another. No Guardian relies on a single contact unless circumstances prevent otherwise, because every contact is in some way compromised: The closer they are to the target, the less likely they are to be unbiased, and vice versa. At the top level of unreliable but close, they might be other Mages from the target's Caucus or cabal. More distant, they might be members of the Mage's cult (if they have one), or spirits they deal with regularly. At the most distant level, you might have people who hang out in the same places as the Mage or who live near them or even just the squirrels that live in the trees outside their sanctum.<br /> <br /> Contacts can also be spies. Sleepwalkers or young apprentices chosen to spy on a target on certain nights, or spirits bound by spells into following and observing. The latter are great when dealing with Moros because the odds of them being detected is pretty much nil.<br /> <br /> Omens, meanwhile, are signs and portents that aren't obviously connected to the unAwakened but which to the mind of a Mage bear ill tidings. For example, if the trees around the Thyrsus's sanctum start getting sick, or a lot of not-so-nice spirits are seen skulking around the neighbourhood, the Guardian knows <i>something</i> is up and can begin a more thorough investigation. Omens are the characteristic signals in the world left by dark deeds; the ripples made by evil. They might also just be changes in the target's behaviour. A strongly religious Mage suddenly not going to temple anymore, for example.<br /> <br /> No omen is proof of malefica but they're good warning signs to start paying closer attention.<br /> <br /> Once a Guardian's radar is pinged by a contact reporting something unusual or an ill omen marking their radar, <i>then</i> they start to look closer. That's when they might start to break the Lex for the sake of their curiosity; stalking the target in the target's own territory; breaking into a sanctum to rifle through their belongings; using spells to scry the target or sneak into their Oneiros, etc.<br /> <br /> This is the important point because Guardians aren't just watching you constantly with their scrying windows; they're looking for unusual behaviour, deviations from the norm, etc. It's once those behaviours get strange enough or are tied to odd enough coincidences (the Counselor started to go to a new basement bar two weeks before the attempt on the Hierarch's life; coincidence?) that the Guardian decides to act.<br /> <br /> A Guardian is not there when a Mage causes a Paradox, typically, or commits any unWise magical act. Instead, they look for the telltale signs; the odd behaviours caused by a Bedlam; the dire omens caused by an Anomaly; the raw destruction caused by a Havoc. Then they track the strangeness back to its source.<br /> <br /> Once that happens, it's time to give some advice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T08:29:01-08:00","id":1011510,"title":"","content":"What all of my previous post means in actual gameplay is that your PCs can be targeted by the Guardians whenever you feel it is justified, as strange omens and informants on their own behaviours draw a Guardian or two to their doorstep. They might not even have actually <i>done</i> anything unWise to warrant it; the Guardians might simply notice other behaviours.<br /> <br /> The Guardians can't logically punish every Paradox. Minor ones are common enough and the consequences thereof are usually not related to the Abyss (a critical spell coming unwound in a time of crisis is usually about as dire as many Havocs get). Unless someone accidentally levels a building with a miscalculated fireball, the Guardians probably never hear of most.<br /> <br /> If a Mage <i>does</i> cause a Paradox, and manages to contain it without suffering Bedlam or some similar abnormality, the Guardians probably don't notice then, either. The Guardians tend to view those who contain a Paradox successfully as more responsible than those that don't, and the results of containing a Paradox successfully are <i>usually</i> not that severe.<br /> <br /> When a Mage <i>does</i> cause a big Paradox, the response of the Guardians is usually not so nice. If the Consilium has causing so severe a Paradox as a punishable offense, as many do, they'll demand the offender offer themselves up for punishment (if the person has otherwise good standing) or drag them before the Hierarch themselves (if not). If the Consilium <i>doesn't</i> have punishments for such offenders, or the Guardians simply don't trust the person enough, what follows is Guardian-style rough justice. For offenders with extenuating circumstances (and there are not many that would meet the Guardians' standards), they might simply levy a heavy penance for the deed. The rest end up sent to whatever next life awaits them.<br /> <br /> If a Consilium has one, this is a job for the Interfector, who can deal out such punishments without violating the Lex.<br /> <br /> These sorts of instances are rare, though. Most Mages, if they don't contain their Paradoxes, receive a stern warning from their local Guardian and change their ways. If they keep violating if flagrantly to little consequence, they might be challenged to a Duel Arcane. If they cause something nasty to happen, the Guardians won't bother with a trial.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> But Paradoxes aren't the only negative behaviours that draw Guardian attention. While the Guardians theoretically target any violation of Wisdom, there are three acts besides Paradox that draw their attention:<br /> <br /> 1. Left-Handed practices.<br /> 2. Exposing the Mysteries to Sleepers.<br /> 3. Self-aggrandizement.<br /> <br /> The Guardians are always on the look-out for any of these. The investigation tactics aren't that different for any of them, except the latter (you don't really need to look too hard to spot a ladder-climber; they <i>want</i> to be seen as often as not). Any Mage suspected of any of these behaviours will be investigated and the results handed over to the Consilium once the case is air-tight.<br /> <br /> If the Guardians can't prove beyond a shadow of a doubt that someone is performing Left-Handed magic or exposing the Mysteries, but they're certain that they are, well... Sometimes the Lex needs to be shunned for the sake of the greater good. Sins for a just end and all.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> I'm not sure how many questions that answered, but... That's all I have in me for now.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T09:07:01-08:00","id":1011522,"title":"","content":"Guardians are basically as able as you want. When designing your setting, &quot;how impotent or potent are Guardians?&quot; is one of major questions you need to ask yourself. In some places, they can't do much using official channels, and are like annoying preachers that just won't shut up about how you are damaging your soul and will try to convert you to proper behavior by evangelization. In other, they might be scary, decisive and murderous. <br /> I personally feel that Paradox is most interesting when it *does* happen, so I tend to drift towards settings where Consilium doesn't care about your Paradox as long as you don't do something major, like endangering another Mage or ruining some important project. Sleepers? Please, who cares about Sleepers. <br /> Then again, I feel that most fun setting for what we run is a Consilium that is passively dickish (won't tell you to kick dogs, but also won't care if you are putting dogs on fire unless you are doing that to pet of another member).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T13:18:07-08:00","id":1011628,"title":"","content":"Really good setting advice there folks","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Placeholder","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset","name":"MercSet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11731_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T13:34:22-08:00","id":1011637,"title":"","content":"I want to point out only one more thing - Guardians <i>are not</i> official law arm of Consillium, Sentintels are. Guardians are weird looking, cult like 'security fetishes' that brings evidence to local Ruling Council and it's Conciliors that dispatch Sentinels actions. Of course, Sentinels can be more pro-active, but by general design, they should work on behalf of Consiliors and Hierarch that are concerned on some signs most often Guardians collected.<br /> <br /> It's one of the reasons that Guardians are following Lex Magica until they don't - cause they would need to wait for proper decision making on things they think are direct danger to Pentacle community.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T17:34:57-08:00","id":1011755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1011468-naughty-pc-s-and-the-guardians-when-do-the-gotv-step-in-and-what-do-they-do?p=1011510#post1011510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> While the Guardians theoretically target any violation of Wisdom, there are three acts besides Paradox that draw their attention:<br /> <br /> 3. Self-aggrandizement.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, what? Since when have the Guardians been concerned about a mage that is promoting himself inside his own caucus?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T17:50:49-08:00","id":1011761,"title":"","content":"Since always? Two of their tenets are &quot;All thrones are false; all souls are flawed&quot; and &quot;Punishment answers pride&quot;. The core book itself notes that the Guardians see it as their duty to &quot;undermine charismatic leaders, expose the faults of wise sages, and force mages to doubt one another&quot;.<br /> <br /> There's a reason the Guardians would be purged if the full extent of their operations came to light.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T17:57:28-08:00","id":1011764,"title":"","content":"Ironic, or fitting, considering their whole secret heresy of the Hieromagus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T18:25:36-08:00","id":1011769,"title":"","content":"Fitting mostly, any potential Heiromagus is tested via assassination. Obviously, someone who can die can't be the Heiromagus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T18:44:22-08:00","id":1011774,"title":"","content":"What exactly does count as exposing Mysteries to Sleepers? Is it literally only mortals who suffer Quiescence, do Hunters count?<br /> <br /> The way its being discussed makes them sound like a cult in fear for the End Times who show up when things are blatantly going wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12243-dreaming-cat","name":"Dreaming Cat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T19:50:04-08:00","id":1011796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dreaming Cat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1011468-naughty-pc-s-and-the-guardians-when-do-the-gotv-step-in-and-what-do-they-do?p=1011774#post1011774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The way its being discussed makes them sound like a cult in fear for the End Times who show up when things are blatantly going wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>All the Orders are cults, and yes the Guardians are there to prevent End Times. Ideally they would act before things get to the 'blatantly going wrong' part by getting rid of mages who would get to that point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T21:37:28-08:00","id":1011840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dreaming Cat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1011468-naughty-pc-s-and-the-guardians-when-do-the-gotv-step-in-and-what-do-they-do?p=1011774#post1011774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What exactly does count as exposing Mysteries to Sleepers? Is it literally only mortals who suffer Quiescence, do Hunters count?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hunters are mortals and they suffer Quiescence so I imagine that yes they do. Just because they're a pain in the ass doesn't mean they don't count. Well...usually.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T09:00:18-08:00","id":1012028,"title":"","content":"Thanks. I didn't know the orders were all cults though, I figured they were governing bodies couched in philosophy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12243-dreaming-cat","name":"Dreaming Cat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T10:12:17-08:00","id":1012054,"title":"","content":"They are that too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T11:49:50-08:00","id":1012088,"title":"","content":"The Orders are mystery cults, criminal conspiracies, shadow governments, and more, all rolled into one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T12:33:48-08:00","id":1012107,"title":"","content":"... but they started as Mystery Cults - it's their most important core identity. I advise to read <i>To the Strongest</i> chapter from <b>Dark Eras</b> - it nicely highlight how Orders come to being and role of newly founded Guardians of Veil come to be. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T12:48:32-08:00","id":1012725,"title":"","content":"So, this thread got me thinking creatively, and as I stand in line for what can only be called my breakfast at 3 PM, I figure I might as well write to keep away the hunger pains.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> Dossier - o to ooooo<br /> <br /> Prerequisite: Guardians of the Veil Status o, Trained Memory (GotV, pg 46) or Eidetic Memory<br /> <br /> You maintain a dossier; a collection of mental documents on the Awakened in your region. This might take many forms but word association codes and memory palaces are common enough methods to be considered the norm. Many Guardians incorporate details into poems.<br /> <br /> Having a dossier allows the Mage to make appropriate rolls (Int + Wits or Composure) to recall details about who a given Mage is, even if they've never met before, as the Mage remembers some details from their information network. They add their Dossier dots as a bonus to this roll.<br /> <br /> In addition to general information, every Guardian who maintains a dossier also has deeper details. Once per session per dot of Dossier, the Guardian in question may gain the Informed Condition about a given Mage or local Caucus, representing the deep insights the Mage has. Other Awakened are often surprised and disturbed when a Guardian they've never met can recite their home address.<br /> <br /> (Note: Informed is not omniscient. The Condition should give the Guardian leverage or an angle to investigate, not solve the mystery instantly.)<br /> <br /> Drawback: Your Dossier requires up-keep by both yourself and others. Your character must faithfully both maintain good standing with their Caucus and contribute information to their superiors' own Dossiers. Falling out of favour can mean losing dots from this merit, or even losing it entirely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T14:35:32-08:00","id":1012783,"title":"","content":"I like this, though I would probably make it less &quot;a thing only Guardians do&quot;, and more of &quot;things Guardians can do easier/cheaper&quot;*. Also would add that certain factors, like obscurity, information nose, smoke-screen and That-Merit-Which-Makes-You-Disappear-From-Face-Of-The-World-God-What's-Its-Name bestow appropriately large penalty to the dice roll.<br /> <br /> *<br /> For example, by adding some requirement that's more XP-intensive than GotV status which can be replaced by GotV1.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 12-05-2016, 05:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T14:39:05-08:00","id":1012786,"title":"","content":"Occultation, and thanks a lot for making me forget it too.<br /> <br /> Yeah, the ST should feel free to apply penalties to the roll based on that.<br /> <br /> Edit: And yeah, anyone can do this theoretically, but Dossier is Guardians only because it represents them not only doing it really well but that they actively reinforce their souls by doing so. Anyone can develop a network of spies and informants, but the Guardians get A-Beats for doing so (via the Informed Condition).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T07:55:03-08:00","id":1015673,"title":"","content":"With the recent passing of actor Ron Glass, I'm reminded that sometime the best way to answer questions and illustrate points is to use a well known example from fiction...<br /> <br /> This example only works if you translate things from the Firefly universe into Awakening.<br /> <br /> Shepherd Book (Ron Glass) from <i>Firefly</i> and <b>Serenity</b> is a good example of a Guardian of the Veil. He's a man with a very mysterious past, possessed of a strange set of skills. He joins the crew of the Serenity and finds a home (his cabal). His job is to be the Conscience of the crew, to remind them that they are still human beings and have an obligation to respect life and empathy and justice. In this way aims to prevent acts of Hubris and falls of grace. When the situation arises, he knows secret words, procedures, and protocols that enable the crew to navigate around the machinations of other Guardians. He knows so much, in fact, that it scares the rest of his cabal -- especially when they see how efficient he is in killing. So, you can see how a Guardian of the Veil might operate when it comes to his own cabal and dealing with threats and forces from outside the people he's sworn to protect.<br /> <br /> Giles from <i>Buffy</i> (Anthony Stewart Head) is also another good example of a Guardian of the Veil to me. This becomes especially clear in the season finale of the story involving elder god Glory and stuff... But anyway... Giles is this guy who appears very much like a Mysterium, until push comes to shove, right? When people are teetering on the edge of darkness, he's there to smack them back to the right side. Likewise, when people succumb to Hubris, he's there to smack them down and remind them of their obligations as a human being. As a Watcher, it's his duty to guide, teach, and protect the Chosen One so that she can fulfill her destiny. But the most Guardian of the Veil thing he does is at the end of Season 5, when they realize that the only way to stop the Hell god Glory is be killing her human vessel/prison, her brother Ben. Ben is an innocent and unwilling participant in this and he begs for his life, he even says something along the lines of &quot;Buffy wouldn't do this!&quot; or something, to which Giles replies, &quot;I know. She's not a killer.&quot; And then Giles suffocates Ben with his bare hand, watching the light go out in his eyes. And Giles saves the day by protecting the Wisdom of the Scooby Gang, taking the sacrifice unto himself.<br /> <br /> Now, those aren't the only examples, or even the most analogous examples, of Guardians of the Veil. In Changeling, they are the Winter Court, in Vampire, they are the Invictus... Stuff like that. There are lots of things to draw from when you're thinking about the Guardians of the Veil so that you're not making them caricatures of homicidal spies (Jason Bourne/James Bond). I think it's really hard to make the Guardians of the Veil look like protagonists and that's intentional.<br /> <br /> They are the bad guys ... until they're not. Then you're glad they are there.<br /> <br /> On of my mage characters used to have a quoted opinion about the members of each Order... sort of a holdover from Classic WoD where everything had a negative opinion about someone else. :-)<br /> She said this of the Guardians of the Veil: <i>&quot;Trust them to do their duty -- and nothing else.&quot;</i><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/346-troy","name":"Troy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}